  If you use this analysis or its reproducibility code, cite the version or
  commit used and the underlying papers and datasets relevant to your work.
  See docs/references.bib and ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md for original-source credits.
title: Additional white dwarf colour candidates from public spectra
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Moriwaki
    given-names: Shota
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-18'
url: https://github.com/dj-thank/pale-yellow-green-white-dwarf-candidate
repository-code: https://github.com/dj-thank/pale-yellow-green-white-dwarf-candidate
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Reproducible public-spectrum analysis identifying two additional pale
  yellow-green white dwarf colour candidates, with pink and unusual yellow
  comparison candidates. The objects and their atmospheric classifications
  are previously known; the potentially new quantity is their calculated
  human-vision chromaticity. This is an exploratory, unreviewed research note
  with ChatGPT-assisted analysis, not a claim of worldwide priority or new
  atmospheric physics. The software licence is Apache-2.0; original prose is
  CC BY 4.0, and third-party data, figures and references retain their own terms.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - white dwarfs
  - public spectra
  - chromaticity
  - CIE 1931
  - Gaia
  - DESI
  - reproducible research
